= render 'shared/breakthrough_page', page_title: 'The Turnip Network', current_page: 'The Turnip Network', page_subtitle: 'Seamless integration and communication between Baldrick boards', document_title: 'The Turnip Network - Baldrick Board Integration', meta: ['Board-to-board networking', 'No code required', 'Works with FPP'] do
  p.lead One of the guiding principles of the Baldrick Boards ecosystem is simple: make life easier.

  .prose
    p We knew people would soon have more than one Baldrick Board in their setup, so we created a clever little networking layer to let them chat to each other and share info.

    h2
      span.hk
        span.bar
        span.annot Features
      | What the Turnip Network does

    .spec-grid
      .spec
        span.ic
          svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9"
            circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"
            path d="M12 2v4M12 18v4M2 12h4M18 12h4"
        h4 Discoverability
        p See every Baldrick Board on your network along with its IP, firmware version and current state.
      .spec
        span.ic
          svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9"
            path d="M4 12h16M8 8l-4 4 4 4M16 8l4 4-4 4"
        h4 Test sync
        p Get boards of the same type marching in step — perfect when you've got props dotted round the garden and you want them all lighting up together.
      .spec
        span.ic
          svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9"
            path d="M12 2v4M5 7l3 3M19 7l-3 3M5 17l3-3M19 17l-3-3M12 18v4"
        h4 FPP discoverability
        p
          | Your boards go hunting for FPP installs on your network, giving you instant interactive fun with buttons or
          = link_to 'Turniputs', breakthroughs_turniput_path
          |  — all without writing a single line of code.
      .spec
        span.ic
          svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9"
            path d="M12 6v6l4 2M22 12a10 10 0 1 1-20 0 10 10 0 0 1 20 0z"
        h4 More on the way
        p Update sharing, time sync and a few other surprises are all in the pipeline.

    figure.figure
      .fimg
        = image_tag 'baldrick8/web-interface-turnip-network.png', alt: 'Turnip Network screen in the Baldrick web interface'
      figcaption The Turnip Network view in the Baldrick web interface — every board on your show network, at a glance.

    .callout.info
      span.ic
        svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
          circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"
          path d="M12 16v-4M12 8h.01"
      div
        span.lbl Good to know
        p.bd
          | The Turnip Network is Baldrick once again going the extra mile to make your lights easier, smarter and a lot more fun. Pair it with
          = link_to 'Turniput inputs', breakthroughs_turniput_path
          |  for visitor-triggered effects without touching a line of code.

    h2
      span.hk
        span.bar
        span.annot Keep reading
      | Related breakthroughs

    .next-grid
      = link_to breakthroughs_turniput_path, class: 'next-card' do
        .top
          span.kind Breakthrough
          span.go →
        h4 Turniput
        p Physical inputs that trigger effects across your show network.
      = link_to breakthroughs_kluster_path, class: 'next-card' do
        .top
          span.kind Breakthrough
          span.go →
        h4 The Kluster
        p Group boards together for coordinated control and testing.
      = link_to breakthroughs_cunningfx_path, class: 'next-card' do
        .top
          span.kind Breakthrough
          span.go →
        h4 CunningFX
        p Advanced effects and scheduling built into the Baldrick ecosystem.
      = link_to breakthroughs_path, class: 'next-card' do
        .top
          span.kind Index
          span.go →
        h4 All breakthroughs
        p Explore everything that makes Baldrick boards a bit special.

section.cta
  .wrap
    h2 Ready to wire up your show?
    p Pick a Baldrick controller and let the Turnip Network handle the rest.
    .cta-btns
      = link_to boards_path, class: 'btn btn-bone' do
        | Explore the range
        span.ar →
      = link_to where_to_buy_baldrick_boards_path, class: 'btn btn-clear' do
        | Where to buy
